  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4a95033faff4a4271a77a8f3b84af233, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 3 Questions
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HokkienQuizQuestionBank
  questions:
  - question: "Why is \u62C5\u4ED4\u9762 also called \u5EA6\u5C0F\u6708\u62C5\u4ED4\u9762?"
    choices:
    - It was created by a person named Xiao Yue
    - It was a celebration food that people ate during the small months
    - It was a dish that fisherman carried on poles to sell during the small months
    - It originated from a ferry crossing called Xiao Yue
    choiceExplanations:
    - This is made up.
    - This is made up.
    - "\u62C5\u4ED4\u9762 (Danzai noodles) are noodles in a pork and shrimp-head broth, topped with shrimp, minced pork, egg and bean sprouts. They are also known as \u5EA6\u5C0F\u6708\u62C5\u4ED4\u9762, which translates to \u201Cnoodles on a carrying pole to get through the small months\u201D. Months with frequent typhoons are called \u201C\u5C0F\u6708\u201D (small months). During these months it was hard to go out to sea, so fishermen carried noodles on poles and sold them for a living. The noodles helped them get through the small months, which gave \u5EA6\u5C0F\u6708\u62C5\u4ED4\u9762 its name."
    - This is made up.
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
  - question: Which of the following means allergy?
    choices:
    - "\u8FC7\u654F"
    - "\u6599\u7406"
    - "\u725B\u8089"
    - "\u4E0D\u8981"
    choiceHokkienRomanizedTexts:
    - "K\u00F2e-b\u00EDn"
    - "Li\u0101u-l\u00ED"
    - "G\u00FB-bah"
    - "M\u0304-\u00E0i"
    choiceAudioResourcePaths:
    - HokkienQuizAudio/level3_allergy
    - HokkienQuizAudio/level3_cooking
    - HokkienQuizAudio/level3_beef
    - HokkienQuizAudio/level3_dont_want
    choiceExplanations:
    - This means allergy in Hokkien.
    - This means "cook" in Hokkien.
    - This means "beef" in Hokkien.
    - This means "I don't want..." in Hokkien.
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
  - question: "What is \u8089\u5706?"
    choices:
    - A Taiwanese dumpling made of starch and rice flour, filled with meat and vegetables
    - A dish that fisherman carried on poles to sell during the small months
    - A Taiwanese meat ball that is served in a meat and vegetable broth
    - A Taiwanese dumpling made from wheat flour, filled with meat and vegetables
    choiceExplanations:
    - "\u8089\u5706 (bah-o\u00E2n) is a translucent dumpling made of sweet potato starch and rice flour, filled with pork, bamboo shoots and mushrooms. It is steamed or deep-fried and served with a sweet and savory sauce."
    - "This describes \u62C5\u4ED4\u9762 (Danzai noodles) from the first question, not \u8089\u5706."
    - "This describes pork ball soup (\u8D21\u4E38\u6C64), not \u8089\u5706."
    - "\u8089\u5706 is not made from wheat flour. Its chewy, translucent skin comes from starch and rice flour."
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
